#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""relogin: sign the glide.vc ChatGPT account into the guardian's own Chrome profile, by hand, once.

The glide.vc guardian browser (chatgpt-guardian-glide-browser) lives on a private Xvfb display, so the owner cannot
type a password into it. This helper is the human part of the `glide-chatgpt-login` finish step (module.toml):

  relogin check   exit 0 = the glide.vc account is signed in, 1 = it is not (or cannot be told), 2 = usage/config
  relogin check --live
                  like check, but ONLY the browser's answer counts: exit 0 solely when the browser shows the right
                  domain; an unreachable browser is retried within CHATGPT_RELOGIN_ACCOUNT_TIMEOUT, then exit 1
                  (never the marker). The glide guardian unit runs it as ExecStartPre, so the sender never starts
                  while the browser is signed in to another account.
  relogin check --refuse-other
                  the home guardian's start check (CHATGPT_RELOGIN_DOMAIN and CHATGPT_RELOGIN_DEVTOOLS_PORT from its unit): exit 1
                  ONLY when the browser shows a signed-in account whose email domain is another one. Signed out, an email
                  domain that is not visible, or a browser that cannot be asked (no DevTools answer, no chatgpt.com tab: a
                  restarted browser has none, within CHATGPT_RELOGIN_ACCOUNT_TIMEOUT) are exit 0, so this check can never keep
                  the guardian down for want of a tab, which `check --live` would.
  relogin run     stop the glide.vc guardian units, open the SAME profile in a visible Chrome window on the real
                  desktop, wait until that window is closed, start the units again in dependency order and verify

`run` takes a per-profile lock first (CHATGPT_RELOGIN_LOCK_DIR; profile-sync's `pull` takes the same one), so the two never
stop the units or open the profile at once.

`run` in order: (1) stop chatgpt-guardian-glide, then -observer, then -browser (the display unit and everything of
the `home` account are never touched); (2) open <profile> with the module's Chrome wrapper on the WAYLAND_DISPLAY /
DISPLAY of the calling shell (ozone auto, start page https://chatgpt.com/auth/login, no DevTools port); (3) wait
until no process uses that --user-data-dir any more. Chrome is single-instance per profile: a second launch hands
over to the running instance and exits at once, so the wait follows the processes that hold the profile (the
command line `--user-data-dir=<profile>` of every Chrome process, and the SingletonLock owner), never only the
launched pid; (4) start -browser, -observer, -guardian; (5) verify, within CHATGPT_RELOGIN_VERIFY_TIMEOUT: the three
units are active and the journal of the guardian shows a `"health": "connected"` line since the start, then ask the
browser which account it is signed in to. Whatever happens after step 1 (Chrome fails to open, Ctrl+C, the terminal
is closed) the units are started again.

`check` rule, no question to the owner, nothing secret printed (only `ok` and an email DOMAIN):
  1. Ask the running browser. Through its DevTools port (module option glide_port, default 9223) take a chatgpt.com
     tab and evaluate `fetch('/api/auth/session')` in it; the page script returns only {signed in?, domain of the
     email}, so the address, the cookies and the access token never leave the browser. Done = signed in with the
     domain `glide_email_domain` (module option, default glide.vc). Another domain or signed out = NOT done, and
     the answer of the browser wins over any marker.
  Only tabs on the real origin https://chatgpt.com count (a look-alike host never runs the page script).
  2. The browser cannot be asked (units stopped, no DevTools answer, no chatgpt.com tab, an unreadable answer such
     as a challenge page): fall back to the marker file ~/.local/state/ubuntu-tweaks/chatgpt-guardian-glide-login,
     and SAY that it could not ask. Done = the marker exists. The marker is "a re-login window was shown to the
     owner, the stack came back healthy AND the browser showed the glide.vc domain" (written by `run` only after
     step 5, with that domain; a `run` that cannot read the account fails and writes nothing). It cannot see a later
     logout: rule 1 does.

Environment (all optional; tests and throwaway experiments set them so the real session is never touched):
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_PROFILE         profile dir            default ~/.local/share/agent-tools/chatgpt-guardian/profiles/glide.vc
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_CHROME          Chrome (wrapper)       default: the module option `chrome` as install.sh reads it ("user" =
                                  ~/.local/bin/chatgpt-guardian-chrome, else that absolute path, default /usr/bin/google-chrome)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_CHROME_ARGS     extra Chrome flags (shell syntax), e.g. --headless=new
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_URL             start page             default https://chatgpt.com/auth/login
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_SYSTEMCTL       command (shell syntax) default "systemctl --user"
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_JOURNALCTL      command (shell syntax) default "journalctl --user"
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_GUARDIAN_UNIT / _OBSERVER_UNIT / _BROWSER_UNIT    defaults chatgpt-guardian-glide, -observer, -browser
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_DEVTOOLS_PORT   default: module option glide_port, else 9223
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_DOMAIN          email domain the account must have (like glide_email_domain; wins over the module option)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_MARKER          default ~/.local/state/ubuntu-tweaks/chatgpt-guardian-glide-login
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_STOP_TIMEOUT    seconds to stop the units / free the profile (default 120)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_VERIFY_TIMEOUT  seconds for the units and the health line of step 5 (default 180: the guardian polls once a minute)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_ACCOUNT_TIMEOUT seconds to wait for a chatgpt.com tab to answer after the restart (default 30)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_PROBE_TIMEOUT   seconds one question to the browser may take in all (default 40: finish gives `check` 60)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_POLL            seconds between polls (default 1)
  CHATGPT_RELOGIN_LOCK_DIR        where the per-profile lock lives (default ~/.local/state/ubuntu-tweaks/chatgpt-guardian-locks)
Module options come as JSON in UBUNTU_TWEAK_MODULE_CONFIG; the language in UBUNTU_TWEAK_LANG (ru or en);
UBUNTU_TWEAK_FINISH_DRY_RUN=1 makes `run` print what it would do and change nothing.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 not done / failed, 2 usage or configuration, 130 interrupted.
"""

